# Architecture Governance (SIS)

> **Source of truth:** `ARCHITECTURE-STACK.md` → Rules → `architecture:validate` → Tests → CI.  
> Cursor assists; **Validator + CI enforce.**

## When User Asks to Create a Feature / Model / Class

**STOP.** Do not default to Laravel CRUD:

```text
❌ app/Models/Teacher.php + Controller with DB/Eloquent
```

**DO** this workflow:

1. Read `.cursor/skills/application-feature/SKILL.md`
2. Run or follow `php artisan sis:make-feature {Context}`
3. Domain Entity + Value Objects first
4. Command/Query + Handler + DTO/Result
5. Repository port only if needed
6. Infrastructure Eloquent adapter (`*Record` in Infrastructure/Persistence)
7. Thin Controller delegates to Handler
8. Tests + `php artisan architecture:validate --fitness`

## Eloquent vs Domain Entity

| Layer | Class | Role |
|-------|-------|------|
| Domain | `Student` entity | Business rules, `canEnroll()` |
| Infrastructure | `StudentRecord` | PostgreSQL persistence |
| Legacy | `app/Models/*` | Migrate away — no new business logic |

## Dependency Direction (enforced)

```text
Controller → Application Handler → Domain ← Infrastructure
```

Forbidden:
- Domain → Illuminate, Application, Infrastructure, Http
- Application → Http, Infrastructure impl, Eloquent, DB
- Controller → DB, Eloquent, business rules

Verify: `php artisan architecture:graph`

## Intelligence Module

Same rules — no Eloquent in Controllers or Application handlers.

Use Application/Intelligence Commands, Queries, DTOs, Contracts (ports).

## Definition of Done

See `.cursor/architecture/FEATURE-DONE.md` before marking feature complete.

## Short User Prompts Are OK

User may say: "أنشئ Feature تسجيل طالب" — architecture comes from Rules + Skill + Validator, not a long prompt.
